From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:52:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: bound the unsafe string calls in the client, cgame
 and ui

strcpy, strcat, sprintf and unterminated _snprintf/_vsnprintf calls in
src/client, src/client_mp, src/cgame, src/ui and src/ui_mp write
without knowing how large the destination is. Part 3 of 4 for upstream
issue 8.

The replacements are the engine's own bounded forms (I_strncpyz,
I_strncat, Com_sprintf, Com_sprintfPos) and C99 snprintf/vsnprintf,
each given the destination's size. No MSVC *_s functions, so the code
stays portable.
